{"author":{"id":"127a58c7f014820991be95805df42525db12c92e2d7319d04d4df105a9aa3444"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1788112101,"nonce":"G8KGhnKbsPlHJUKfAqR1PSXWzmw=","title":"1.4 rwa CLI (rimworld-tools)","message":"Wave 1 — substrate. Depends: 1.1 (protocol), 1.3 (advance UX). Agent-facing.\n\n## Goal\n`rwa` — the CLI the agent (and rwtest) actually uses. Thin, scriptable,\njq-able; zero game logic client-side.\n\n## Context (read first)\n- DESIGN.md §Architecture §Observation (context budgets, jq philosophy)\n- 1.1's protocol spec + code; analyzerbridge/CLAUDE.md drive-it section\n- `rimworld-tools/log-watcher/watcher.py` (house python style)\n- `_RimWorld-Testing/run-testing.sh` + 0.1's run-agent.sh (watch integration)\n\n## Scope\n- `rwa \u003cverb\u003e [--arg val …] [--json|--pretty]`: write command file, wait for\n  result (timeout; on stale status.json heartbeat say \"game not running\" and\n  how to start it), print. Non-zero exit on ok:false.\n- `rwa journal --since \u003cseq\u003e [--type …]`; `rwa tail` (follow).\n- `rwa watch [on|off]`: toggle Hyprland special workspace visibility + raise/\n  lower fps cap (mechanism per 0.1 findings).\n- Transcript mode: every command+result mirrored into a session run-dir\n  (playbook post-mortems and rwtest reports both consume these).\n- Lives in `rimworld-tools` (new top-level `rwa/` or beside log-watcher —\n  worker's call); env override for the bench path (RIMWORLD_VAULT pattern).\n\n## Invariants\nMachine output is always valid JSON; pretty mode never invents data; CLI adds\nno game semantics (that belongs in-mod or in specs 2.x).\n\n## Open questions (worker's)\nArg syntax conventions per verb; how much pretty-printing lives here vs digest\nstrings from 2.1; transcript dir naming.\n\n## Acceptance\n- ping/status/advance round-trip from a shell; documented jq pipeline example\n  works as pasted.\n- Game-down produces a clear, fast failure with guidance.\n- A short scripted session leaves a complete, replayable transcript dir.","files":null}]}